{
  "description": "U6 start: three starts per new Chromium profile (start 1 cold: first start after an engine update, 2 and 3 warm), first layout of example.com. Sites (engine_runs in this order): 0 bc4b179 before U6, 1 main with U6 (crash stack, early loading), 2 link with -Oz, 3 the giant functions with less inlining (the LLInt interpreter loop with -Os, wasm-opt limits the growth of a function by inlining to 16384 of its size units instead of 409600), 4 WebCore with -Os, 5 PTHREAD_POOL_DELAY_LOAD. U6 is also pool A (8 Workers before main(), 4 spare at start); PoolB and PoolD have 3 before main() and 9 spare at ready or at the first paint. Rule correction for U6 against E0, rule lever for sites 2 to 5 and the pool against U6, on the warm first layout; ready and the cold start only as tables. DelayLoad, PoolB and PoolD also have to pass pool6.json (CNN). Runs per group: about 49 (C LAN), 66 (C mobile) and 33 s (S LAN) per arm and run from GH 39319116414, 8 arms, so 30, 24 and 30 runs take about 3.7, 3.9 and 2.6 h with the setup of six sites",
